# Criterion 6 - mason make flutter_starter_setup with a custom application id
#
# A clean copy of this branch (rsync, minus .git / build / .dart_tool /
# docs/verification) was generated into a scratch directory and the brick run
# against it with:
#
#   package_name      acme_app
#   application_id    com.acme.mobile
#   ios_bundle_id     com.acme.mobileApp
#   app_display_name  Acme App
#   strip_sample_features / include_* : defaults (nothing stripped)
#
#   $ mason get && mason make flutter_starter_setup -c vars.json --on-conflict overwrite
#   Renamed Dart package to acme_app
#   Moved MainActivity to match com.acme.mobile
#   Moved MainActivityTest to match com.acme.mobile
#   Updated iOS PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER to com.acme.mobileApp
#   Updated patrol config to com.acme.mobile
#   Rewrote identifiers in 21 platform file(s)
#   Setup complete. Next: flutter pub get && flutter analyze && flutter test
#
# Then, over the GENERATED project:
#
#   grep -rn 'com\.example\|flutterStarter\|flutter_starter' . \
#     --exclude-dir=.dart_tool --exclude-dir=build --exclude-dir=docs \
#     --exclude-dir=bricks --exclude-dir=.claude --exclude-dir=.mason
#
# Output follows, unfiltered and unedited apart from shortening the absolute
# scratch path in mason-lock.json. Every remaining hit is intentional:
#
#   - README.md / CONTRIBUTING.md : project prose.
#     bricks/flutter_starter_setup/README.md states Markdown is not rewritten.
#   - mason.yaml / mason-lock.json : the brick's own manifest, which names the
#     brick. Renaming it would break `mason make`.
#   - pubspec.yaml:94 : a comment pointing at the brick's hook.
#   - test/tooling/check_env_assets_test.dart:14 : `name: flutter_starter` inside
#     a synthetic pubspec STRING literal that the test feeds to
#     findBundledEnvAssets. Not a project identifier; rewriting it would change
#     nothing the test asserts.

